     "result_text_tail": "rket growth is confirmed at 42% a year, the pop-up grew 18% a week, and the plan stays positive if it misses any one of its four targets. The problem is that it needs all four together.\n\n**Decisions I made in your absence** (all listed on the last slide):\n1. **Profit per order.** The pack doesn't define the founders' \"contribution profit\", so I show it both before and after the dark-store cost. The conclusion holds either way.\n2. **Cash need.** I read the $9.5M as the whole company's need to month 18, which is the most favourable reading for the plan. If it comes on top of today's $0.4M monthly burn, the plan needs about $16.7M, more than the cash.\n3. **Pop-up growth.** The daily order rates (about 180 to 410) assume steady 18% weekly growth. Customer payback leaves out months 1\u20132 and churn after month 3, which the pack has no data on.\n4. **Format.** I made it an editable PowerPoint file with the charts drawn as ordinary shapes, written as a recommendation to the board.\n\nThe sandbox blocked PowerPoint, Keynote and Chrome from rendering the file, so I haven't seen the real slides. Instead I drew PNG previews from the same layout code, checked text fit using real Arial measurements, and reviewed every slide that way. It's worth flicking through the deck in PowerPoint once before it goes out.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/` and `./build/`:\n- Parcelbird_Now_board_deck.pptx\n- `deck.py`, `model.py` and `lib.py` (rerun `python3 build/deck.py` to rebuild)\n- `preview/` (the slide PNGs)"
    }
